msgstr "Defining Language Strings"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_notifications.rst:199
msgid ""
"Next we can start defining some language strings that will be used by the "
"notification. This specific language file contains all possible language "
"strings that can be used in a notification. You can remove any strings that "
"you will not need."
msgstr ""
"Next we can start defining some language strings that will be used by the "
"notification. This specific language file contains all possible language "
"strings that can be used in a notification. You can remove any strings that "
"you will not need."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_notifications.rst:204
msgid ""
"This language file will be included during a user's setup later on in this "
"tutorial, meaning that they will be globally available. However, there are a "
"few strings that are only needed in the :abbr:`UCP (User Control Panel)`. "
"Ideally these strings should be defined in a separate file, namely :class:"
"`info_ucp_extension.php`. Using this naming convention (:class:`info_ucp_*."
"php`) will automatically include it only in the UCP. But for the sake of "
"this tutorial, they are all being defined in this one language file."
msgstr ""
"This language file will be included during a user's setup later on in this "
"tutorial, meaning that they will be globally available. However, there are a "
"few strings that are only needed in the :abbr:`UCP (User Control Panel)`. "
"Ideally these strings should be defined in a separate file, namely :class:"
"`info_ucp_extension.php`. Using this naming convention (:class:`info_ucp_*."
"php`) will automatically include it only in the UCP. But for the sake of "
"this tutorial, they are all being defined in this one language file."

